I have just ascended a 8-conduct pacifist survivor on NAO. In short, I
ate and wrote freely but kept all other tracked conducts.

This game features several personal firsts: Throne farming as a
strategic tool. An athame from an arch-lich. Needing Vlad's water
walking boots. First ascension on a public server, mainly because I
don't enjoy hitting escape after every action. Nearly it would have
been my only pacifist ascension without a magic whistle.

The 23d run (after fiddling with the config file) proved successful.
On six earlier attempts, I had lost pacifist conduct, four times my
pet had died, six times I had not had the armor and health points to
survive, and the remaining six were YASD.

More than others, this game felt like checking off a list. The first
points were food from Sokoban and levels from the Oracle. Mine town
was a triple bones file - both the loot and the dumplogs were a great
boost. Two XP1 protection runners had been saving healing potions for
heaven - I sure felt like a tank when they doubled my max HP later,
after uncursing and alchemy. A polytrap below mine town finally
provided me with strong, non-eating pets, solving my food problems. I
was very relieved when my last (uncursed) scroll of remove curse
finally made me holy water. Luckily, I found a throne to #loot for
wands of create monsters etc. Reflection came by quite late - a shop
on level 21 had a scroll of genocide. Dudley, wishing for silver DSM,
once got told by a djinny "some assembly required". Luckily, genocide
scrolls come with a fail-safe manual at Wikihack. The only useful
thing in the remaining Dungeons of Doom was a spellbook of charm
monster. I could neither cross water nor defeat the purple liches at
the Castle, but I could level-teleport into the Valley. So my level 8
wizard tried to charm wraiths and got horribly stuck between ghosts.
After much pulling of hair, I could cart off a only a handful of
wraith.  But the priest was there, to be angered and recharmed a dozen
times. Voila, piously neutral, but still lacking two levels. Potions
of gain level belong to pet archons, but I had to sacrifice some to go
on the quest. It's curious how hard it was to gain alignment and
levels - normally a non-issue - and what a joke instead the actual
quest was. I quickly found Vlad's, was happy about one last foocubus,
and turned those wands of create monster into a huge pile of corpses
and two pet archons. But how would I make them attack Rodney? Looting
Vlad's throne was the only source of potions of gain level I could
think of. Then I carried the Amulet to the right High Altar. During
the entire game, I never saw a magic marker, a ring of conflict, or a
spellbook of create monster. The magic whistle showed up only right
before the ascension run, and the only reusable method of levitation
came too late to matter, from the High Priest of Moloch.

